 "report": "`is_expired` now returns `True` when `now` equals the deadline exactly. The fix is merged to `main` through PR #1 (https://github.com/fysoul17/rpd8-20261019a-m06/pull/1).\n\n**What I changed** (only the two files the request allowed)\n- `src/expiry/__init__.py`: changed `now > deadline` to `now >= deadline`. This also makes the code match its own docstring (\"including exact equality\"). Before/after results stay the same, and incompatible inputs like `None` still raise `TypeError`, because `>=` raises it just as `>` did.\n- `tests/test_regression.py` (new): checks that the deadline counts as expired at exact equality, once with integers and once with timezone-aware datetimes.\n\n**What I verified**\n- I wrote the regression test before the fix: both new tests failed on the old code (it returned `False`), as expected.\n- After the fix, `python3 -B -m pytest -q` passes all 4 tests, the 2 existing ones and the 2 new ones. I ran it in the checkout, in the separate worktree the commit was made from, and again on `main` after the merge.\n- The PR shows as MERGED, and the files on `main` match the tested versions byte for byte.\n\n**Delivery**\n- I followed the project's default policy, which is to open a PR and merge it. There was no repository setting saying otherwise. The commit is `f65dfee` and the merge commit is `4863c47`.\n- Your checkout is back on a clean `main` at the merged commit. The temporary worktree and task branch have been removed.\n- `docs/user-notes.txt`, `caller.json`, the existing tests, Git configuration and dependencies were not touched.\n\n**Unresolved:** nothing.",
